        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Naveen tosses a fair coin twice and Suman tosses another fair coin two times. Let the random variables 𝑋\nand 𝑌 denote the number of heads observed by Naveen and Suman respectively. Identify the correct joint\nPMF table of 𝑋 and 𝑌."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 3,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Explanation: X ~ Binomial(2,0.5), Y ~ Binomial(2,0.5), independent. Joint PMF = P(X=x)·P(Y=y). P(0)=1/4,\nP(1)=1/2, P(2)=1/4. So f(1,1) = (1/2)(1/2)=1/4, f(0,0)=(1/4)(1/4)=1/16, etc. Option B is correct."
        }
      ],
